<title>BELGIUM: Freighters fly 35.8pc of '96 Europe airlines' cargo.</title>
<headline>Freighters fly 35.8pc of '96 Europe airlines' cargo.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>All-cargo aircraft accounted for 35.8 percent of global freight tonne-kilometres (FTKs) transported by European carriers on international routes in 1996, figures from the Association of European Airlines (AEA) showed.</p>
<p>This compared to 35 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>European airlines carried 23.6 billion FTKs on international routes last year, an increase of 4.8 percent on 1995, AEA added.</p>
<p>AEA defines international traffic as the sum of international short-/medium-haul and total long-haul services.</p>
